    "content": "D. John Sauer is the 49th and current Solicitor General of the United States, having assumed the position in April 2025. Based in the Department of Justice, this official acts as the federal government's lead litigator before the U.S. Supreme Court, overseeing government cases, filing briefs, and often referred to as the \"tenth justice\". Key Responsibilities and Role Supreme Court Litigation: Responsible for conducting and supervising all Supreme Court cases on behalf of the U.S. government. Case Selection: Determines which cases the federal government will appeal to the Supreme Court. Amicus Briefs: Decides when the government will intervene or file amicus curiae (friend-of-the-court) briefs in cases. Legal Representation: Argues cases on behalf of the Executive Branch before the Supreme Court. Office Context Location: Part of the Department of Justice, based in Washington, D.C.. Significance: Known for having a high success rate in having cases accepted by the Supreme Court, serving as a \"gatekeeper\" for federal litigation. Predecessor: Elizabeth B. Prelogar served as the 48th Solicitor General from 2021 to 2025.",
